      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 4. Claim Rewrite\n",
        "\n",
        "My strongest original claim could have been interpreted too broadly as:\n",
        "\n",
        "> \"The model identifies declining content.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "I would rewrite this claim more carefully as:\n",
        "\n",
        "> **\"The analysis measured whether current-state content and search signals could prioritize observations associated with an observed declining trend. In the tested evaluation, the transparent Week-4 rule-based baseline performed better than Logistic Regression on Precision@10 and Precision@50. The resulting prioritization should therefore be treated as directional decision-support evidence for human review, not as a definitive prediction of future search decline.\"**\n",
        "\n",
        "This wording matches what the experiment actually measured.\n",
        "\n",
        "It avoids claiming causation, future prediction, or knowledge of Google's ranking system."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qR3yl5rt-t0O"
      },
      "id": "qR3yl5rt-t0O"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 5. Ranked Recommendations\n",
        "\n",
        "Based on the measured baseline signals, I would prioritize human review in the following order.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 1. Stale + Low CTR\n",
        "\n",
        "These observations satisfy both baseline signals.\n",
        "\n",
        "Review:\n",
        "\n",
        "- content freshness\n",
        "- search intent alignment\n",
        "- title and description presentation\n",
        "- usefulness of the page\n",
        "\n",
        "Recommended action:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Review first.**\n",
        "\n",
        "## 2. Stale Content\n",
        "\n",
        "These observations have been unchanged for at least 90 days.\n",
        "\n",
        "Review whether:\n",
        "\n",
        "- information is still current\n",
        "- examples remain relevant\n",
        "- statistics need updating\n",
        "- search intent has changed\n",
        "\n",
        "Recommended action:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Review for possible refresh.**\n",
        "\n",
        "## 3. Low CTR Despite Visibility\n",
        "\n",
        "These observations have sufficient impressions, appear within positions 1–20, and have CTR below 0.5%.\n",
        "\n",
        "Review:\n",
        "\n",
        "- title relevance\n",
        "- description relevance\n",
        "- search intent\n",
        "- SERP context\n",
        "- whether the result clearly communicates the page's value\n",
        "\n",
        "Recommended action:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Review CTR opportunity.**\n",
        "\n",
        "## 4. Monitor\n",
        "\n",
        "Observations that do not satisfy either signal should not automatically be treated as failures.\n",
        "\n",
        "Recommended action:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Continue monitoring and investigate when additional evidence appears.**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "L4sWNzl7-vp2"
      },
      "id": "L4sWNzl7-vp2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 6. Error Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "The Logistic Regression model should not be treated as a definitive classifier.\n",
        "\n",
        "False positives are observations that the model ranked or classified as likely declining but that were not observed as declining.\n",
        "\n",
        "False negatives are observations that were observed as declining but were not identified strongly by the model.\n",
        "\n",
        "The error analysis is important because a large number of errors indicates that the four selected signals do not perfectly separate the observed classes.\n",
        "\n",
        "Human review therefore remains necessary."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e1QO0TjT-xQ8"
      },
      "id": "e1QO0TjT-xQ8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "grouped_error_df = X_test_grouped.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "grouped_error_df[\"actual_decline\"] = y_test_grouped.values\n",
        "grouped_error_df[\"model_probability\"] = grouped_probability\n",
        "\n",
        "grouped_error_df[\"model_prediction\"] = (\n",
        "    grouped_probability >= 0.5\n",
        ").astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "grouped_error_df[\"error_type\"] = np.select(\n",
        "    [\n",
        "        (\n",
        "            (grouped_error_df[\"actual_decline\"] == 1) &\n",
        "            (grouped_error_df[\"model_prediction\"] == 0)\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        (\n",
        "            (grouped_error_df[\"actual_decline\"] == 0) &\n",
        "            (grouped_error_df[\"model_prediction\"] == 1)\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    [\n",
        "        \"false_negative\",\n",
        "        \"false_positive\"\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    default=\"correct\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\n",
        "    grouped_error_df[\"error_type\"].value_counts()\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "display(\n",
        "    grouped_error_df[\n",
        "        grouped_error_df[\"error_type\"] != \"correct\"\n",
        "    ].head(10)\n",
        ")"
      ],
