      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 10. Conclusion\n",
        "\n",
        "This project investigated whether current-state search and content signals could be used to prioritize potentially declining content for human review.\n",
        "\n",
        "A transparent rule-based baseline was created using staleness and low CTR despite visibility.\n",
        "\n",
        "The Week-5 experiment compared this baseline with Logistic Regression using days since last update, 90-day impressions, average position, and CTR.\n",
        "\n",
        "On the original held-out evaluation, the baseline measured:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Precision@10: **70.0%**\n",
        "- Precision@50: **54.0%**\n",
        "\n",
        "Logistic Regression measured:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Precision@10: **40.0%**\n",
        "- Precision@50: **46.0%**\n",
        "\n",
        "The measured result therefore did not show an improvement from Logistic Regression over the simpler baseline.\n",
        "\n",
        "The Week-6 grouped validation adds a more conservative client-level validation perspective and reduces the possibility of client overlap between training and testing.\n",
        "\n",
        "The resulting system should therefore be treated as a transparent prioritization and decision-support framework rather than an autonomous content optimizer.\n",
        "\n",
        "The key lesson is that model complexity should earn its place through measured improvement.\n",
        "\n",
        "In this experiment, the simpler baseline remained the stronger measured approach."
      ],
