      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 1. Two Paper Findings + My Methodology Questions\n",
        "\n",
        "The FlyRank research paper presents findings about search/content performance using observational data. I use the paper as an example of how findings should be interpreted carefully rather than treated as automatically causal.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding 1\n",
        "\n",
        "The paper reports an observed relationship between its analyzed search/content signals and performance outcomes.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Methodology question\n",
        "\n",
        "Where exactly does the outcome label come from?\n",
        "\n",
        "I would want to understand how the outcome was defined, which fields were used to construct it, and whether any outcome-related information could also appear in the model inputs. A clearly defined label makes it easier to understand what the result actually measures.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is a constructive question because the interpretation of any model result depends heavily on how the outcome was created.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Finding 2\n",
        "\n",
        "The paper reports performance differences between groups or conditions in the analyzed data.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Methodology question\n",
        "\n",
        "Does the validation design support the strength of the claim?\n",
        "\n",
        "I would check whether the validation split prevents related observations from appearing in both training and evaluation data, and whether the evaluation setup matches the intended real-world use.\n",
        "\n",
        "A stronger validation design can help determine whether an observed pattern is likely to generalize beyond the exact observations used during analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "These questions do not reject the paper's findings. They are the same type of questions I should ask of my own analysis."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "GBc1HpFs98jv"
      },
      "id": "GBc1HpFs98jv"
    },
