    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Recreate the Week-4 Baseline\n",
        "\n",
        "The baseline uses the same two signals as the original analysis:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Staleness: at least 90 days since the last update.\n",
        "2. Low CTR despite visibility: at least 500 impressions, average position between 1 and 20, and CTR below 0.5%.\n",
        "\n",
        "The baseline assigns:\n",
        "\n",
        "- 2 points for staleness\n",
        "- 1 point for low CTR despite visibility\n",
        "\n",
        "The score therefore ranges from 0 to 3."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "-pXgbjsU-TQT"
      },
      "id": "-pXgbjsU-TQT"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "def baseline_score(data):\n",
        "    stale = (\n",
        "        data[\"days_since_last_update\"] >= 90\n",
        "    ).astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "    low_ctr_visible = (\n",
        "        (data[\"impressions_90d\"] >= 500)\n",
        "        &\n",
        "        (data[\"avg_position\"].between(1, 20))\n",
        "        &\n",
        "        (data[\"ctr\"] < 0.5)\n",
        "    ).astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return (\n",
        "        2 * stale +\n",
        "        1 * low_ctr_visible\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "random_baseline_scores = baseline_score(\n",
        "    X_test_random\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "random_baseline_p10 = precision_at_k(\n",
        "    y_test_random.values,\n",
        "    random_baseline_scores.values,\n",
        "    10\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "random_baseline_p50 = precision_at_k(\n",
        "    y_test_random.values,\n",
        "    random_baseline_scores.values,\n",
        "    50\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Week-5 baseline Precision@10:\",\n",
        "      round(random_baseline_p10 * 100, 2), \"%\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Week-5 baseline Precision@50:\",\n",
        "      round(random_baseline_p50 * 100, 2), \"%\")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "6KqbzFm3-VGI",
        "outputId": "81218b31-955f-4eae-eb92-78d393b06188"
      },
      "id": "6KqbzFm3-VGI",
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Week-5 baseline Precision@10: 70.0 %\n",
            "Week-5 baseline Precision@50: 54.0 %\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Client-Grouped Split — After\n",
        "\n",
        "For the validation audit, I keep all observations from the same client together.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is more conservative for a use case where the model may eventually be applied to clients that were not represented during training.\n",
        "\n",
        "The grouped split reduces the possibility that the model benefits from seeing related observations from the same client in both training and testing.\n",
        "\n",
        "The client identifier is therefore used for grouping only and is not provided to the model."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "V1nckpJC-Xdg"
      },
      "id": "V1nckpJC-Xdg"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.model_selection import GroupShuffleSplit\n",
        "\n",
        "gss = GroupShuffleSplit(\n",
        "    n_splits=1,\n",
        "    test_size=0.20,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "train_idx, test_idx = next(\n",
        "    gss.split(X, y, groups=groups)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train_grouped = X.iloc[train_idx]\n",
        "X_test_grouped = X.iloc[test_idx]\n",
        "\n",
        "y_train_grouped = y.iloc[train_idx]\n",
        "y_test_grouped = y.iloc[test_idx]\n",
        "\n",
        "groups_train = groups.iloc[train_idx]\n",
        "groups_test = groups.iloc[test_idx]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Grouped training rows:\", len(X_train_grouped))\n",
        "print(\"Grouped test rows:\", len(X_test_grouped))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Training clients:\", groups_train.nunique())\n",
        "print(\"Test clients:\", groups_test.nunique())\n",
        "\n",
        "overlap = set(groups_train) & set(groups_test)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Client overlap:\", len(overlap))\n",
        "\n",
        "assert len(overlap) == 0, \"Client leakage detected!\"\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Grouped split check: PASSED\")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "1k4VS_HR-Y7Z",
        "outputId": "e06fd415-6ca8-44cd-c3d0-4238650d8b3e"
