    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 6. Error Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "The Logistic Regression model should not be treated as a definitive classifier.\n",
        "\n",
        "False positives are observations that the model ranked or classified as likely declining but that were not observed as declining.\n",
        "\n",
        "False negatives are observations that were observed as declining but were not identified strongly by the model.\n",
        "\n",
        "The error analysis is important because a large number of errors indicates that the four selected signals do not perfectly separate the observed classes.\n",
        "\n",
        "Human review therefore remains necessary."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e1QO0TjT-xQ8"
      },
      "id": "e1QO0TjT-xQ8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "grouped_error_df = X_test_grouped.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "grouped_error_df[\"actual_decline\"] = y_test_grouped.values\n",
        "grouped_error_df[\"model_probability\"] = grouped_probability\n",
        "\n",
        "grouped_error_df[\"model_prediction\"] = (\n",
        "    grouped_probability >= 0.5\n",
        ").astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "grouped_error_df[\"error_type\"] = np.select(\n",
        "    [\n",
        "        (\n",
        "            (grouped_error_df[\"actual_decline\"] == 1) &\n",
        "            (grouped_error_df[\"model_prediction\"] == 0)\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        (\n",
        "            (grouped_error_df[\"actual_decline\"] == 0) &\n",
        "            (grouped_error_df[\"model_prediction\"] == 1)\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    [\n",
        "        \"false_negative\",\n",
        "        \"false_positive\"\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    default=\"correct\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\n",
        "    grouped_error_df[\"error_type\"].value_counts()\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "display(\n",
        "    grouped_error_df[\n",
        "        grouped_error_df[\"error_type\"] != \"correct\"\n",
        "    ].head(10)\n",
        ")"
      ],
