      "source": [
        "# 7. Feature Interpretation\n",
        "\n",
        "Logistic Regression coefficients provide a directional interpretation of how the selected features contributed to the fitted model.\n",
        "\n",
        "They should not be interpreted as causal effects.\n",
        "\n",
        "A positive coefficient means that higher standardized values of that feature were associated with a higher model score for the observed decline class.\n",
        "\n",
        "A negative coefficient means the opposite within the fitted model.\n",
        "\n",
        "The coefficients describe this model and this dataset. They should not be generalized into claims about how Google's ranking system works."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "_QQsRQD5-4YZ"
      },
      "id": "_QQsRQD5-4YZ"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
