        "# 8. Limitations & Honest Framing\n",
        "\n",
        "Several limitations apply to this analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "First, the observed decline outcome comes from the supplied dataset's `trend_direction` definition. It should not be treated as a universal definition of content failure.\n",
        "\n",
        "Second, this is observational analysis. A higher declining rate among stale or low-CTR-visible observations does not prove that those signals cause decline.\n",
        "\n",
        "Third, the Logistic Regression model did not outperform the Week-4 baseline in the original Week-5 ranking evaluation.\n",
        "\n",
        "Fourth, the model intentionally uses only four current-state signals. Other signals may contain useful information, but adding them without careful validation could introduce leakage or overfitting.\n",
        "\n",
        "Fifth, the random Week-5 split may provide a less conservative estimate when observations from the same client can occur in both training and testing. The grouped Week-6 split addresses this concern.\n",
        "\n",
        "Finally, this analysis does not prove how Google's search or ranking systems work.\n",
        "\n",
        "The appropriate interpretation is therefore:\n",
        "\n",
        "**observed, measured, directional, and decision-support evidence.**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "jzLC1Vjb-8O7"
      },
      "id": "jzLC1Vjb-8O7"
